  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Genesis",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "The descendants of Noah are Japheth, whose descendants are Gentiles; Ham, whose descendants include the Canaanites; and Shem, of whom came Peleg (in whose days the earth was divided).",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now these are the generations of the sons of Noah, Shem, Ham, and Japheth: and unto them were sons born after the flood.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "IE genealogical lines."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Gen. 5:32."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sons of Japheth; Gomer, and Magog, and Madai, and Javan, and Tubal, and Meshech, and Tiras.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Ezek. 38:6."
          },
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Ezek. 38:2; Rev. 20:8."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "Ps. 120:5; Ezek. 27:13; 38:2."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Gomer; Ashkenaz, and Riphath, and Togarmah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "Ezek. 27:14; 38:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Javan; Elishah, and Tarshish, Kittim, and Dodanim.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "1 Chr. 1:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "Ezek. 27:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Septuagint and 1 Chr. 1:7: Rodanim."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "By these were the isles of the Gentiles divided in their lands; every one after his tongue, after their families, in their nations.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "HEB From these."
          },
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "OR coasts, continents."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Gentiles."
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "TG Nations."
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "TG Family."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Ham; Cush, and Mizraim, and Phut, and Canaan.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "1 Chr. 1:8 (8–10); Abr. 1:21, 25 (20–25)."
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "IE Ethiopians, Egyptians, Libyans, and Canaanites. See 1 Chr. 1:4–23."
          },
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "IE Egypt. D&C 136:22; Abr. 1:23 (20–25); 2:21."
          },
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Nahum 3:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Cush; Seba, and Havilah, and Sabtah, and Raamah, and Sabtecha: and the sons of Raamah; Sheba, and Dedan.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Cush begat Nimrod: he began to be a mighty one in the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "1 Chr. 1:10; Ether 2:1 (1, 4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He was a mighty hunter before the Lord: wherefore it is said, Even as Nimrod the mighty hunter before the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "Micah 5:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the beginning of his kingdom was Babel, and Erech, and Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "OR (later) Babylon."
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "Gen. 11:2; 2 Ne. 21:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Out of that land went forth Asshur, and builded Nineveh, and the city Rehoboth, and Calah,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Resen between Nineveh and Calah: the same is a great city.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Mizraim begat Ludim, and Anamim, and Lehabim, and Naphtuhim,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "1 Chr. 1:11 (11–16)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Pathrusim, and Casluhim, (out of whom came Philistim,) and Caphtorim.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 56,
            "text": "Gen. 21:34; 1 Chr. 1:12; 2 Ne. 12:6; 19:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Canaan begat Sidon his firstborn, and Heth,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Moses 7:7 (6–8); Abr. 1:22 (21–22)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Jebusite, and the Amorite, and the Girgasite,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Hivite, and the Arkite, and the Sinite,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Arvadite, and the Zemarite, and the Hamathite: and afterward were the families of the Canaanites spread abroad.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "Gen. 12:6; 13:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the border of the Canaanites was from Sidon, as thou comest to Gerar, unto Gaza; as thou goest, unto Sodom, and Gomorrah, and Admah, and Zeboim, even unto Lasha.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "Gen. 20:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "These are the sons of Ham, after their families, after their tongues, in their countries, and in their nations.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Unto Shem also, the father of all the children of Eber, the brother of Japheth the elder, even to him were children born.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Gen. 14:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 115
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The children of Shem; Elam, and Asshur, and Arphaxad, and Lud, and Aram.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "1 Chr. 1:17 (17–25)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And the children of Aram; Uz, and Hul, and Gether, and Mash.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "Job 1:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Arphaxad begat Salah; and Salah begat Eber.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And unto Eber were born two sons: the name of one was Peleg; for in his days was the earth divided; and his brother’s name was Joktan.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "IE Division."
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "TG Earth, Dividing of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 53
          },
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 126
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joktan begat Almodad, and Sheleph, and Hazarmaveth, and Jerah,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Hadoram, and Uzal, and Diklah,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Obal, and Abimael, and Sheba,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ophir, and Havilah, and Jobab: all these were the sons of Joktan.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 22,
            "text": "Gen. 2:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 49
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And their dwelling was from Mesha, as thou goest unto Sephar a mount of the east.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "These are the sons of Shem, after their families, after their tongues, in their lands, after their nations.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "These are the families of the sons of Noah, after their generations, in their nations: and by these were the nations divided in the earth after the flood.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 85,
            "text": "TG Nations."
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "HEB from."
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 116,
            "text": "TG Nations."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 6,
            "end": 9
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
